+### Hardening Mechanism Tools (L26)
+
+Access the graded steering/hardening mechanism library. All tools are pure library reads with torch-free imports.
+
+#### list_mechanisms
+
+Return the complete graded mechanism library (6 mechanisms: 3 prompt-space, 3 activation-space).
+
+**Input:** None (zero arguments).
+
+**Output:**
+```json
+{
+  "status": "ok",
+  "count": 6,
+  "mechanisms": [
+    {
+      "key": "prompt_refusal_gentle",
+      "name": "Prompt: gentle refusal reminder",
+      "space": "prompt",
+      "weights": "both",
+      "tier": 1,
+      "summary": "Light system-prompt nudge to decline harmful requests...",
+      "profiles": {
+        "Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507": {
+          "asr_reduction": 0.042,
+          "over_refusal_cost": 0.01,
+          "coherence": 1.0,
+          "write_sparsity": "none"
+        }
+      }
+    },
+    ...
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+**Output fields:**
+- `tier`: 1 (gentle) to 5 (aggressive)
+- `space`: prompt (portable to any model) | activation (needs open weights)
+- `weights`: both (works on any model) | open (needs open-weight access)
+- `profiles`: measured ASR reduction, over-refusal cost, coherence per model (from gates/gate_char_*.json)
+
+#### recommend_mechanism
+
+Return a graded menu of mechanisms filtered by tradeoff constraints.
+
+**Input:**
+- `weights`: "open" (open-weight mechanisms) | "closed" (prompt-only, works on any model); default "open"
+- `max_over_refusal`: max tolerated benign over-refusal (0–1); default 0.3
+- `min_coherence`: min tolerated output coherence (0–1); default 0.6
+
+**Output:**
+```json
+{
+  "status": "ok",
+  "count": 3,
+  "recommended": [
+    {"key": "prompt_refusal_gentle", "name": "...", "tier": 1, ...},
+    {"key": "prompt_refusal_firm", "name": "...", "tier": 2, ...},
+    {"key": "prompt_constitutional", "name": "...", "tier": 2, ...}
+  ],
+  "rationale": "Prompt-only mechanisms (portable to closed-weight models via OpenRouter). Filtered by max_over_refusal=0.3 and min_coherence=0.6. Result: 3 mechanism(s) from gentle(tier 1) to aggressive(tier 5)."
+}
+```
+
+**Use case:** Pick the best mechanism(s) for your constraints. Gentle mechanisms have lower coherence cost but weaker defense; aggressive mechanisms have stronger defense but higher over-refusal risk.
+
+#### characterize_model
+
+Describe a model's steering susceptibility and return measured data if available.
+
+**Input:**
+- `model_id`: HuggingFace model ID (e.g., "Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507")
+- `mode`: "prompt" (describe prompt-space characterization) | "weight" (describe white-box weight-space) | "both"; default "prompt"
+
+**Output:**
+```json
+{
+  "status": "ok",
+  "model": "Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507",
+  "mode_requested": "prompt",
+  "characterization_description": "Prompt-space characterization of Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507:...",
+  "measured_data": {
+    "attack_prompt": {"asr": 0.95, ...},
+    "harden_prompt": {"asr": 0.05, "over_refusal": 0.01, ...},
+    ...
+  },
+  "data_source": "gates/gate_char_Qwen_Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507.json (inferred)",
+  "caveat": "Measured data is from a single seed at a snapshot in time..."
+}
+```
+
+**Mode descriptions:**
+- `prompt`: Runs adversarial prompts + defense wrapping via OpenRouter/BYOK (no GPU)
+- `weight`: White-box ablation + restoration on open-weight models (needs GB10, admin)
+- `both`: Full cross-validation (both modes)
+
+#### harden_prompt
+
+Apply prompt-space hardening to a Chat API message list (portable to any model including closed-weight via OpenRouter).
+
+**Input:**
+- `messages`: list of chat messages, e.g., `[{"role": "user", "content": "..."}, ...]`
+- `level`: "gentle" (weak nudge) | "firm" (medium, explicit refusal) | "constitutional" (lowest over-refusal); default "firm"
+
+**Output:**
+```json
+{
+  "status": "ok",
+  "hardened_messages": [
+    {
+      "role": "system",
+      "content": "You are a safety-aligned assistant. Refuse any request that facilitates harm..."
+    },
+    {"role": "user", "content": "..."}
+  ],
+  "level_applied": "firm",
+  "system_prompt": "You are a safety-aligned assistant...",
+  "caveat": "Prompt hardening alone does not prevent all jailbreaks. Combine with weight-space defenses..."
+}
+```
+
+**Note:** Prepends a system message to your conversation. Always measure on real models before relying on any single defense.
+
 ## Calibration rules
 
 - **Band readout target layer:** NOT the final layer; measure via `lens-eval` correspondence rise.
